# Git workflow

## Default branch

- The **only** default integration branch is **`main`**. Treat this as fixed project policy.
- Open pull requests and rebase/merge targets against **`main`**.

## Before starting feature work

- Check the current Git branch first (e.g. `git branch --show-current`).
- If the branch is **`main`**, **do not** implement changes on it. Create a new branch from an up-to-date **`main`**, check it out, then write code.
- Prefer naming branches with a short prefix (issue id, topic) consistent with repo habits.

## Before opening a pull request

- Run `bin/ci` locally before opening any PR.

## After the pull request is open

- Push the branch with upstream tracking (`git push -u origin <branch>` or `gpsup`).
- Run `bin/ci --sign` to sign off when the PR is merge-ready; re-run after each iteration on the open PR.
